menu "Aktualino script secondary (Berry)"

config AKTUALINO_SCRIPT_SECONDARY
    bool "Enable the Berry script secondary (Uptane-signed on-device plugins)"
    default n
    help
        Build the optional Berry script-secondary feature
        (docs/berry-secondary-spec.md): a second, independently-versioned Uptane
        target track that delivers small Berry scripts to a LittleFS partition and
        runs them as a virtual secondary ECU (hardware id "aktualino-lua").

        When DISABLED (the default), none of the Berry runtime or script components
        are compiled, no scripts partition or second ECU exists, and the firmware
        is byte-identical to a build without the feature. Enable it (e.g. per-target
        for the ESP32-S3) to opt in.

        This single switch gates both the aktualino_berry (VM) and, later,
        aktualino_script (secondary logic) components.

endmenu
